[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/3205294311","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2822#issuecomment-3205294311","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2822","id":3205294311,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE86_DOjn","user":{"login":"xsuchy","id":85769,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1NzY5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/85769?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xsuchy","html_url":"https://github.com/xsuchy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xsuchy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xsuchy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xsuchy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xsuchy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xsuchy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xsuchy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xsuchy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xsuchy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xsuchy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-20T09:58:00Z","updated_at":"2025-08-20T09:58:00Z","body":"Text of the exception:\n```\nThis is the file COPYING.modifiedLGPL, it applies to several units in the                                                                                                                        \nLazarus sources distributed by members of the Lazarus Development Team.\nAll files contains headers showing the appropriate license. See there if this\nmodification can be applied.\n\nThese files are distributed under the Library GNU General Public License\n(see the file COPYING.LGPL) with the following modification:\n\nAs a special exception, the copyright holders of this library give you\npermission to link this library with independent modules to produce an\nexecutable, regardless of the license terms of these independent modules,\nand to copy and distribute the resulting executable under terms of your choice,\nprovided that you also meet, for each linked independent module, the terms\nand conditions of the license of that module. An independent module is a\nmodule which is not derived from or based on this library. If you modify this\nlibrary, you may extend this exception to your version of the library, but\nyou are not obligated to do so. If you do not wish to do so, delete this\nexception statement from your version.\n\n\nIf you didn't receive a copy of the file COPYING.LGPL, contact:\n      Free Software Foundation, Inc.,\n      675 Mass Ave\n      Cambridge, MA  02139\n      USA\n```\n\nNote that it is very close to https://spdx.org/licenses/Classpath-exception-2.0.html (but is missing the leading paragraph) or to https://spdx.org/licenses/Independent-modules-exception.html (slightly different wording of second and third paragraph).\n\nI am not sure if we want to alter the markup of one of these exceptions or create a new exception.","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/3205294311/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/3234083855","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2822#issuecomment-3234083855","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2822","id":3234083855,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE87AxDQP","user":{"login":"swinslow","id":678569,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3ODU2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/678569?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow","html_url":"https://github.com/swinslow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-28T16:01:16Z","updated_at":"2025-08-28T16:01:16Z","body":"@xsuchy Thanks for this... I would tend to treat the only relevant \"exception\" text as being the third paragraph from what you submitted above (\"As a special exception, ...\"). I'd tend to treat the first, second and fourth bits as essentially surplus text that identifies e.g. which files the license and exception apply to, but not themselves relevant text.\n\nAs you mentioned, it appears that this paragraph is identical to the _second_ paragraph of https://spdx.org/licenses/Classpath-exception-2.0.html. So an ideal outcome might be if the first paragraph of Classpath-exception-2.0 could be marked as optional.\n\nUnfortunately, I'm not sure it can. That sentence is certainly in the realm of being \"arguably legally substantive legal text\", by defining its view of when portions of GPL apply. So I don't think we can just mark it as optional while treating it as the \"same\" exception.\n\nI think this points towards creating a second instance, e.g. Classpath-exception-2.0-short or something like that. I don't love that naming, but something in that vein might be how to move this forward.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/3234083855/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,